1
00:00:00,495 --> 00:00:02,348
A cat that falls from the twentieth floor

2
00:00:02,352 --> 00:00:04,502
can get hurt less than one that falls

3
00:00:04,352 --> 00:00:05,169
from the seventh.

4
00:00:05,388 --> 00:00:06,895
It sounds like a glitch in the game,

5
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:08,717
but science has an explanation.

6
00:00:09,316 --> 00:00:12,014
In nineteen eighty-seven, vets in New York studied

7
00:00:11,995 --> 00:00:14,181
one hundred and thirty-two cats that had fallen

8
00:00:14,031 --> 00:00:14,954
from buildings.

9
00:00:15,185 --> 00:00:16,562
Ninety percent survived.

10
00:00:17,162 --> 00:00:18,169
And the strangest part:

11
00:00:18,507 --> 00:00:20,646
injuries got worse up to the seventh floor.

12
00:00:20,853 --> 00:00:22,622
After that, they started to drop.

13
00:00:22,853 --> 00:00:24,943
To understand this glitch, let's level up.

14
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:26,212
Level one:

15
00:00:26,277 --> 00:00:27,093
the twist.

16
00:00:27,312 --> 00:00:29,331
In mid-air, the cat bends its body in

17
00:00:29,181 --> 00:00:31,867
half, turns the front end, then the back

18
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:32,974
end, and boom:

19
00:00:33,265 --> 00:00:34,022
feet down.

20
00:00:34,662 --> 00:00:36,229
It can do this because it has a

21
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:39,598
super flexible spine and a floating collarbone that

22
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:41,134
isn't locked to other bones.

23
00:00:41,365 --> 00:00:43,015
It's like its body came with a spin

24
00:00:42,865 --> 00:00:43,336
button.

25
00:00:43,962 --> 00:00:44,588
Level two:

26
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:45,505
top speed.

27
00:00:45,748 --> 00:00:48,636
Because it's light and fluffy, a cat stops

28
00:00:48,498 --> 00:00:50,707
speeding up at around sixty miles per hour.

29
00:00:50,938 --> 00:00:52,922
A person reaches almost double that.

30
00:00:53,528 --> 00:00:55,750
And it hits that speed after falling about

31
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,738
five floors.

32
00:00:57,016 --> 00:00:59,059
From there on, the fall doesn't get any

33
00:00:58,921 --> 00:00:59,690
faster.

34
00:01:00,316 --> 00:01:01,193
Level three:

35
00:01:01,483 --> 00:01:02,335
the parachute.

36
00:01:02,566 --> 00:01:05,216
Once it stops speeding up, the cat relaxes

37
00:01:05,078 --> 00:01:07,645
and spreads its legs like a flying squirrel.

38
00:01:07,864 --> 00:01:09,954
That slows it down and spreads out the

39
00:01:09,804 --> 00:01:10,550
impact.

40
00:01:11,162 --> 00:01:11,681
So:

41
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,062
in a short fall, it hits the ground

42
00:01:13,924 --> 00:01:14,991
still tense.

43
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:17,300
In a long fall, there's time to twist,

44
00:01:17,234 --> 00:01:18,265
relax and glide.

45
00:01:18,907 --> 00:01:20,629
But this story has a final boss.

46
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,188
Cats that died in the fall were almost

47
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:24,212
never taken to the vet.

48
00:01:24,443 --> 00:01:26,748
So the study only saw the survivors.

49
00:01:27,395 --> 00:01:28,867
Cats don't have nine lives.

50
00:01:29,086 --> 00:01:31,331
If you live in an apartment, window screens

51
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,533
are the most important item in this game.

52
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:36,991
So, has your cat ever fallen off something

53
00:01:37,067 --> 00:01:38,979
and just walked away like nothing happened?

54
00:01:39,222 --> 00:01:40,324
Tell me in the comments.
